   "widgets_values": [
    "## Model Links\n\nText encoder only — **no diffusion model needed** for this workflow.\n\n- [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/blob/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors) — 5.2 GB\n- [qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/blob/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors) — 8.9 GB\n\n## Model Storage Location\n\n```\nComfyUI/\n└── models/\n    └── text_encoders/\n        └── qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors\n```\n\n**ClipProj Device Loader** puts it on the GPU you choose — the stock\n`CLIPLoader` only offers `default` and `cpu`. No projection is involved here:\nthe matrix only matters when conditioning a diffusion model.\n\n## Why this node and not another\n\nComfyUI's `SDClipModel.generate()` drops `embeds_info` and never calls\n`build_image_inputs`, so image tokens land at linear positions instead of\nQwen3-VL's 3D mRoPE and get no DeepStack injection. The model then invents a\nplausible description of an image it never saw. This node restores the full path.\n\n## Speed\n\n**~20 tok/s on a 3090**, far below llama.cpp or vLLM: ComfyUI re-casts weights on\nevery forward, which suits diffusion but is costly one token at a time.\n`precision` and the preloaded head mitigate it.\n"
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
